From 07776ec870194a81d83a824f3d48b78aa6582952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jssng-pinetree <james.sng@pinetree-research.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:42:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sandbox): add Solari as a hosted sandbox provider

Adds a Solari Cloud-Hypervisor microVM backend for the sandbox harness, matching
the Blaxel/E2B/Modal provider shape:
- src/agents/extensions/sandbox/solari/ (SolariSandboxClient/Session/State,
  options, timeouts) on the solari-sandbox SDK; lazy import so registration works
  without the extra installed.
- Registered in agents.extensions.sandbox (try-import + __all__).
- pyproject: openai-agents[solari] extra + mypy override.
- docs/sandbox/clients.md: platforms-table row.
- examples/sandbox/extensions/solari_runner.py.

exec -> cmd.run, files -> fs.read/write, exposed ports -> preview_url, workspace
persist/hydrate via tar, interactive PTY via pty.create (cmd+argv over the control
channel), and resume() reattach backed by a full guest memory+device-state snapshot
(durable, cross-host-recoverable subject to a golden/topology compat check).

Verified: zero unimplemented abstract methods; imports + registers in-repo;
live-tested end-to-end against a real Solari microVM (exec/files/ports/PTY and a
pause->serialize->resume round-trip) via the reference at
github.com/solari-sdk/solari-cookbook (integrations/openai-agents).

